.policy "ruff-ruf017-quadratic-list-summation" revision 3
.description "Avoid flattening lists by summing them onto an empty list; it is quadratic, so chain them with itertools instead."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff RUF017: `sum(lists, [])` flattens by adding lists one at a time, copying the total at each step:
// quadratic. The builtin sum, a positional iterable, and an empty list, `[]` or `list()`, as `start` (second
// or `start=`).
//   sum([x, y], [])              ← RUF017  `list(itertools.chain.from_iterable([x, y]))`
//   sum([x, y], start=[])        ← RUF017
//   sum(x, list())               ← RUF017
//   sum([x, y])                  not reported
//   sum(iterable=x, start=[])    not reported: Ruff wants the iterable positional
#include "python/ruff.rr"
param_slot("builtins.sum", "iterable", 0). param_slot("builtins.sum", "start", 1).

.violation RUF017(at: node) code "RUF017"
    "Replace `sum(lists, [])` with `list(itertools.chain.from_iterable(lists))`; summing onto a list copies it at every step (quadratic). Leave it when the input is only a few short lists."
    suppress ruff "RUF017"
RUF017(c) :- ruff_arg(c, 0, _), call_param(c, "start", s), empty_literal(s, "list").
